@page "/"

<PageTitle>Students Affairs</PageTitle>

<h1>Students Affairs</h1>

<p class="lead">
    A sample Blazor Web App (.NET 10, Interactive Auto) built on an n-tier architecture
    with the Unit of Work and Repository patterns over EF Core / SQL Server.
</p>

<div class="row g-3 mt-2">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">Manage students</h5>
                <p class="card-text">Browse, search, sort and page the student register; create, edit and delete records.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/students">Open student list</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">REST API</h5>
                <p class="card-text">The same use cases are exposed under <code>/api/students</code> and documented with Swagger.</p>
                <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary" href="/swagger" target="_blank">Open Swagger UI</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-4 h4">Solution layout</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>StudentsAffairs.Domain</strong> — entities &amp; enums (no dependencies).</li>
    <li><strong>StudentsAffairs.Shared</strong> — DTOs &amp; the <code>IStudentApi</code> contract shared with the WASM client.</li>
    <li><strong>StudentsAffairs.Application</strong> — service layer, repository/unit-of-work interfaces, mapping.</li>
    <li><strong>StudentsAffairs.Infrastructure</strong> — EF Core <code>DbContext</code>, repositories, <code>UnitOfWork</code>, migrations.</li>
    <li><strong>StudentsAffairs.Web</strong> — Blazor host, API controllers, composition root.</li>
    <li><strong>StudentsAffairs.Web.Client</strong> — Blazor WebAssembly UI (pages, forms, HTTP client).</li>
</ul>
